diff --git a/policy/starVLA/README.md b/policy/starVLA/README.md
index 3aa9791..6611325 100644
--- a/policy/starVLA/README.md
+++ b/policy/starVLA/README.md
@@ -29,6 +29,25 @@ The vendored `source_starvla` runtime implements the inference-side contract bel
 
 Released checkpoints should retain their run-directory layout so the runtime can find `config.yaml`, `config.full.yaml`, and `dataset_statistics.json` next to the `checkpoints/` directory. The public data-mixture name is `robodojo_arx_x5_h50_q99`; `robodojo_v21_all_h50_q99` remains supported as a compatibility alias.
 
+## Local Research Extension: Staged Planner Residency
+
+The CARVE project launcher supports a separate local VLM with serialized
+GPU use. `STARVLA_STAGED_RESIDENCY=transfer` is the unchanged default;
+`cpu_mirror` is an opt-in development candidate for eager frozen parameters.
+It keeps immutable CPU copies instead of repeatedly copying unchanged GPU
+weights back. Mutable registered buffers still move normally. This consumes
+additional host RAM and has a one-time preparation cost; it is not quantization
+or a real-time control guarantee. Do not train, merge adapters, mutate weights
+or attach dispatch/compilation hooks while mirrors are active.
+
+Use the project's `scripts/run_robodojo_starvla_nominal.sh` with
+`CARVE_PLANNER_BACKEND=staged_vlm`, a local `CARVE_PLANNER_MODEL`, and the
+explicit residency variable. The launcher exposes the CARVE Python package
+and records the chosen mode. Direct server users must make that package
+importable and pass `--staged-residency cpu_mirror`. Neither flag enables
+Agent actions in a shadow run. Deployment admission and measured results are
+tracked in the project's `docs/plans/ROBODOJO_AGENT_MEMORY_EXECUTION_PLAN.md`.
+
 ## Installation
 
 `install.sh` installs PyTorch 2.6, the upstream requirements, flash-attn, and `source_starvla/` in editable mode into the active environment:
